# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the values are
#   specific to the developer's machine. See:
#   https://stackoverflow.com/questions/21867137/should-i-commit-python-version-file-to-git
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1264, Pipfile.lock should be committed, but Pipfile.lock.prev is not.
#   Pipfile.lock.prev can be generated if you use some versions of pipenv, check context if you want to commit.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock should be committed, but poetry.lock.prev is not.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock should be committed
#pdm.lock

